<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#projectedOnto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01492#stereotype_sunny_weather> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The background of the image shows a beach with the ocean and sky, which is typically associated with sunny weather. The meme uses this context to create a humorous contrast between the expected behavior (wearing sunscreen, a hat, or staying out of the sun) and the actual behavior (wearing a visor, which is not typically associated with sun protection in this context). This juxtaposition is the source of the meme's humor, and it relies on the viewer's understanding of social norms and expectations around beach attire and sun protection."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#temporallyRelatedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#consilientWith> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Emotion> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Emotion Expression elements from the image. Emotion Expression includes: facial expressions, emotional gestures, mood indicators, affective elements, and emotional cues. For each emotional element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'mischievous_smile', 'concerned_expression'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the mischievous smile', 'the concerned expression'), 3) A brief description of the emotional state or expression. Focus on clearly visible emotional indicators that convey feelings or moods. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"mischievous_smile\", \"label\": \"the mischievous smile\", \"description\": \"A knowing, slightly devious smile suggesting mischief or satisfaction\"}"@en .
