<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01492#mapping_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'i don't like the sun so i wear a visor' is mapped onto the visual entity 'woman'. The woman is depicted wearing a visor while standing on a beach, which is a contextually inappropriate setting for someone claiming to dislike the sun. The meme uses this juxtaposition to create an ironic and absurd mapping where the woman's visual presence (wearing a visor on a beach) is interpreted as a literal embodiment of the text's claim. The mapping is established through the direct textual reference to the woman's actions and appearance, creating a humorous contrast between her stated preference and the visual context."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Speech-ThoughtIntegration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text representing character dialogue, thoughts, or internal communication in memes"@en .
