<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01492#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman on a beach wearing a visor, with text overlay stating 'i don't like the sun so i wear a visor.' The scene is framed to highlight her physical appearance, including her skin tone, body type, and the visor she is wearing. The meme uses a juxtaposition of the text and image to create a humorous or ironic effect, implying that the woman's choice of headwear is an unusual or exaggerated response to sun exposure. The overall intent is to elicit laughter or amusement through absurdity, rather than to convey a harmful message. There is no evidence of abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda content. The meme relies on visual and textual contrast to create a comedic effect, and while it may involve a qua-entity (skin tone and body type), it does not target or demean any specific group in a harmful way. The intent is purely for entertainment and does not promote or perpetuate stereotypes or harmful narratives."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dramaticallyIronicalTo> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relationIndex> "14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#verballyIronicalTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01492#woman> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractedFrom> "01492.png" .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#diagonallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:ndab2d21bc577464b81cc1ed472bb7fe6b19 .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#visuallyCompositionCompliantWith> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#OpaqueOverlay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text blocks that completely obscure underlying visual content in memes"@en .
_:ndab2d21bc577464b81cc1ed472bb7fe6b40 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
_:ndab2d21bc577464b81cc1ed472bb7fe6b10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01492#audience_id_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed for a broad, general internet audience familiar with online humor, visual memes, and internet culture. It relies on universal visual tropes (woman on a beach, visor, text overlay) and absurd juxtaposition for comedic effect, making it accessible to viewers without specific cultural or demographic markers. The humor is derived from the incongruity between the text and image, not from niche references."@en .
_:ndab2d21bc577464b81cc1ed472bb7fe6b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:ndab2d21bc577464b81cc1ed472bb7fe6b3 .
