<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Scene> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Scene Composition elements from the image. Scene Composition includes: spatial arrangements, element positioning, scene organization, layout structures, and spatial relationships. For each compositional element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'foreground_focus', 'background_scene'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the foreground focus', 'the background scene'), 3) A brief description of the spatial arrangement and its significance. Focus on how elements are positioned and organized within the scene. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"foreground_focus\", \"label\": \"the foreground focus\", \"description\": \"The girl positioned prominently in the foreground, drawing immediate attention while the fire rages behind her\"}"@en .
