<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01492#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual material of the woman standing on the beach wearing a visor. The meme's humor and irony arise from the user identifying with or imagining themselves in the situation described by the text — 'i don't like the sun so i wear a visor' — and seeing the woman as a representation of that behavior. The projection is implicit, not explicit (no deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you'), but the user is invited to mentally map themselves onto the woman's actions and appearance to understand the joke. The user is projected onto the 'woman' entity, which is the central visual material and the subject of the textual mapping."@en .
