<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#rhythmicallyIntegratedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "rhythmically integrated with"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01492#stereotype_black_skin_tone_and_body_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme relies on the visual presentation of the woman's skin tone and body type to create a comedic effect. This is not inherently harmful, but the combination of these features with the text can activate stereotypes in some contexts, such as associating certain body types or skin tones with laziness, lack of discipline, or being 'too much' for a given situation. The meme's humor is derived from the absurdity of the woman's choice of headwear, which is exaggerated to the point of being ridiculous, and this exaggeration is amplified by the visual markers of her appearance."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#comparativelyPositionedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:ndab2d21bc577464b81cc1ed472bb7fe6b10 .
